{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 24, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e4b-it", "content": "## Lost (and Found) in Japan\n\nJust back from the most incredible trip to Japan! It was a whirlwind of ancient traditions and futuristic vibes – a truly captivating contrast.\n\nMy journey started in Tokyo, a dazzling metropolis. Shibuya Crossing was a sensory overload in the best way possible, and exploring the quirky shops of Harajuku was a highlight. I spent hours wandering through serene gardens and marveling at the vibrant street art.\n\nFrom Tokyo, I took a bullet train to Kyoto. The change of pace was amazing. Kyoto felt steeped in history, with stunning temples like Kinkaku-ji (the Golden Pavilion) and Fushimi Inari Shrine’s thousands of red torii gates. I even participated in a traditional tea ceremony – a wonderfully calming experience.\n\nThe food was, of course, phenomenal. From fresh sushi and ramen to delicate wagashi (Japanese sweets), every meal was a delight. I learned to navigate chopsticks (somewhat successfully!) and embraced the culture of slurping noodles.\n\nBeyond the big cities, I explored smaller towns, soaking in the local atmosphere and enjoying the incredible hospitality. The people were incredibly kind and helpful, even with my limited Japanese.\n\nJapan is a country that truly stays with you. It’s a place of beauty, respect, and endless discovery. I can’t wait to go back!\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "##", "logprob": -1.4305104514278355e-06}, {"token": "▁Lost", "logprob": -0.0012646066024899483}, {"token": "▁(", "logprob": -0.11973774433135986}, {"token": "and", "logprob": -1.1920922133867862e-06}, {"token": "▁Found", "logprob": -0.0013262771535664797}, {"token": ")", "logprob": -0.11968433856964111}, {"token": "▁in", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "▁Japan", "logprob": -0.08475944399833679}, {"token": "\n\n", "logprob": -0.15028037130832672}, {"token": "Just", "logprob": -1.0541269779205322}, {"token": "▁back", "logprob": -